WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.055
[rock music playing]

00:43.043 --> 00:46.464
CHAPTER 1:
I AM A WEB NOVEL WRITER

00:46.547 --> 00:48.549
[Western standoff music playing]

00:52.636 --> 00:55.765
[person 1] Ho has been friends
with Yeon-hui since childhood.

00:55.848 --> 00:56.849
HO
BITTERSWEET HEART

00:56.932 --> 00:58.976
He seems taciturn and nonchalant,

00:59.059 --> 01:01.729
but he's unexpectedly caring,
that's his charm point.

01:02.605 --> 01:04.482
Jin is a college friend of Yeon-hui's.

01:04.565 --> 01:05.691
JIN
RAY OF SUNSHINE

01:05.775 --> 01:08.277
He's so sweet you'd think he's an angel.

01:09.236 --> 01:10.821
Fans are split

01:11.655 --> 01:14.116
between those who support
the Yeon-hui and Ho couple…

01:14.909 --> 01:18.621
and those who support
the Yeon-hui and Jin couple. YeonJin.

01:19.538 --> 01:20.664
But I…

01:22.249 --> 01:24.001
[whimsical music playing]

01:27.463 --> 01:29.965
Didn't I tell you to stay out of my sight?

01:30.049 --> 01:33.260
Every time I see you,
I get so damn irritated.

01:33.344 --> 01:34.345
Why?

01:34.970 --> 01:36.305
Why the hell?

01:36.889 --> 01:38.015
[music stops]

01:39.517 --> 01:41.685
Why the hell couldn't I have
met you sooner?

01:43.312 --> 01:44.772
[person 1] …I'm Team HoJin.

01:44.855 --> 01:47.399
-[romantic music playing]
-You fool.

01:47.483 --> 01:49.485
[person 1] They have no choice
but to hide their feelings.

01:49.568 --> 01:51.821
Look at the way they look at each other.

01:57.076 --> 01:59.078
[phone ringing]

02:01.539 --> 02:02.540
Sorry.

02:04.834 --> 02:06.168
Hello, Dad.

02:06.252 --> 02:07.253
What was that?

02:07.336 --> 02:08.879
[Dad] I'm getting remarried.

02:08.963 --> 02:10.381
To Geum-yeong.

02:10.464 --> 02:13.384
You and Ho will be brothers. [laughs]

02:13.467 --> 02:17.137
You better keep getting along
with each other. [laughs]

02:17.221 --> 02:18.389
[exhales sharply]

02:20.182 --> 02:21.809
-Hold up, hold up.
-[bell rings]

02:23.102 --> 02:25.229
I just can't let
something like this slide.

02:25.312 --> 02:26.981
Are you out of your mind?

02:29.817 --> 02:30.943
Hey! I'm talking to you!

02:32.653 --> 02:33.654
Me?

02:33.737 --> 02:36.490
This is the last episode.
Isn't that right?

02:38.158 --> 02:40.411
-It is.
-And you're gonna ruin it like that?

02:40.494 --> 02:43.455
I've been patient this whole time,
but the story is way too slow.

02:43.539 --> 02:45.499
They don't even realize
they like each other

02:45.583 --> 02:47.877
until the last episode?
That makes no sense.

02:47.960 --> 02:49.962
What's with the random
"they're brothers" twist?

02:50.045 --> 02:51.422
Are you kidding me?

02:51.505 --> 02:55.092
Well, there might be a second season.

02:55.175 --> 02:57.177
[scoffs] Really?

02:57.261 --> 03:00.389
After that mess you wrote,
you're hoping for a second season?

03:00.472 --> 03:03.559
You just caused all this,
and no one wants to read your stuff!

03:03.642 --> 03:04.727
[gasps]

03:04.810 --> 03:06.812
That's so harsh.

03:06.896 --> 03:08.314
Is that her?

03:08.397 --> 03:10.566
The writer who
totally butchered everything,

03:10.649 --> 03:14.153
from characters to narratives,
plots, and plausibility?

03:14.236 --> 03:15.738
[stammers]

03:16.572 --> 03:18.949
[sirens wailing]

03:19.658 --> 03:20.701
Huh?

03:28.292 --> 03:30.002
[officer] Where is she?

03:30.085 --> 03:31.545
-Over there.
-Arrest her.

03:33.464 --> 03:34.924
Hmm?

03:38.052 --> 03:41.263
Freeze! Hands off the keyboard!
Don't touch it!

03:41.347 --> 03:43.223
-[stammers] What…
-I said freeze!

03:43.307 --> 03:45.309
B-But I didn't do anything at all.

03:45.392 --> 03:48.062
Oh, come on. You already know
your writing sucks.

03:49.229 --> 03:51.440
[stutters] Writing a bad novel…

03:53.233 --> 03:54.818
i-isn't a crime, you know!

03:54.902 --> 03:56.779
-Oh, yes it is!
-[whimpers]

03:56.862 --> 03:59.448
Under Article 1, Clause 1
of the Web Novel Act,

03:59.531 --> 04:01.742
-bad writers must be punished.
-What?

04:01.825 --> 04:03.577
-Therefore, Yeo Eui-ju…
-Huh? What?

04:03.661 --> 04:06.997
-…you're under arrest.
-Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh!

04:07.081 --> 04:08.499
Don't do this! Don't do this!

04:08.582 --> 04:12.044
Don't do this! Don't do this!
Don't do this!

04:12.127 --> 04:13.796
[gasps, breathes sharply]

04:13.879 --> 04:15.547
[sighs, grunts]

04:18.592 --> 04:20.427
[sighs, sniffles]

04:20.511 --> 04:21.887
[groans]

04:21.971 --> 04:24.264
I really thought I was getting arrested.

04:24.348 --> 04:25.474
[sighs]

04:25.557 --> 04:27.351
[shudders, sniffles]

04:28.394 --> 04:31.021
PAZER WEB NOVEL PORTAL

04:31.855 --> 04:33.023
[sniffles]

04:34.066 --> 04:35.067
[sighs]

04:38.070 --> 04:39.321
I am…

04:39.405 --> 04:40.948
PAZER WEB NOVEL PORTAL

04:41.031 --> 04:42.449
…a writer.

04:42.533 --> 04:43.575
[sighs]

04:45.119 --> 04:47.287
A writer who specializes in…

04:47.913 --> 04:49.999
BL.

04:50.082 --> 04:51.375
BL: ABBREVIATION OF BOYS' LOVE

04:51.458 --> 04:53.043
PRIZE
WRITING CONTEST

04:54.545 --> 04:55.838
My pen name

04:57.047 --> 04:58.048
is Imuk.

04:59.717 --> 05:01.385
No one reads my stuff.

05:01.468 --> 05:02.845
THEY CAME TOGETHER

05:02.928 --> 05:04.388
No one but me.

05:05.973 --> 05:10.102
The one with two views was just
someone who clicked by accident.

05:10.686 --> 05:13.313
They could've at least left
a hate comment while they were at it.

05:14.398 --> 05:16.608
ZERO REVIEWS

05:16.692 --> 05:17.776
[sniffles]

05:23.782 --> 05:24.783
This is Yeo Eui-do.

05:26.076 --> 05:29.163
He's the only brat
who knows that I write BL novels.

05:29.246 --> 05:30.622
Cola.

05:30.706 --> 05:32.124
YEO EUI-DO
COKE ADDICT BROTHER

05:32.916 --> 05:35.586
He's been blackmailing me with that.

05:38.964 --> 05:41.759
EPISODE 1

05:45.220 --> 05:46.221
[sighs]

05:46.805 --> 05:49.516
What should I write for my next piece?

05:49.600 --> 05:52.728
[groans]
I can't afford another big failure.

06:10.287 --> 06:14.291
[romantic music playing]

06:14.374 --> 06:17.669
[person 1 groans]
Aren't your legs sore? They feel tense.

06:17.753 --> 06:19.129
[person 2] Did you shower?

06:19.213 --> 06:20.672
You smell really nice.

06:20.756 --> 06:22.132
Is that the one I got you?

06:25.385 --> 06:28.680
[person 1] Ooh, you're way too tense. Huh?
You need more stretching.

06:28.764 --> 06:32.184
[person 1, person 3 groaning]

06:32.267 --> 06:33.769
[person 1] Stand up.

06:33.852 --> 06:35.020
Let's loosen up your shoulders.

06:35.104 --> 06:36.355
[person 3] Hey, no, not here!

06:36.438 --> 06:37.981
[person 1] Ugh, let's do it inside, then.

06:38.065 --> 06:40.150
[person 3 stammering] What, no, stop!

06:40.234 --> 06:42.277
Jung, come on, it's still too early!

06:44.988 --> 06:47.324
[person 2] Did you have a good night?

06:47.407 --> 06:49.868
I couldn't sleep one bit because of you.

06:50.410 --> 06:52.037
Because you weren't with me.

06:54.623 --> 06:56.041
So tonight,

06:56.125 --> 06:58.585
-I don't want to sleep alone.
-I don't want to sleep alone.

06:59.920 --> 07:00.921
[chuckles]

07:01.004 --> 07:02.297
Huh?

07:10.973 --> 07:12.432
[person 2] What's with that girl?

07:12.516 --> 07:14.226
Is she here for me?

07:14.309 --> 07:15.561
Wasn't that a boy?

07:15.644 --> 07:17.187
-It was a girl.
-I see.

07:17.271 --> 07:19.273
-How are your eyes?
-They're okay.

07:19.356 --> 07:20.607
What's wrong with Dong-ju?

07:20.691 --> 07:22.734
-He got a cramp.
-Why did Gi-jeon carry him in?

07:22.818 --> 07:23.902
He says it's for training.

07:23.986 --> 07:25.320
[door opens]

07:26.155 --> 07:28.657
CHAPTER 2: DO YOU KNOW
WHY STUDENTS WEAR UNIFORMS?

07:28.740 --> 07:30.826
EUI-JU'S HOUSE - SHIN,
YOON-JU, EUI-JU, EUI-DO, SUNI

07:35.038 --> 07:38.876
Ma, did the twins and their family
who used to live at the big white house

07:38.959 --> 07:40.002
move away?

07:41.295 --> 07:42.504
Did they?

07:42.588 --> 07:46.425
Well, it looks like someone else moved in.
It's just a bunch of guys now.

07:46.508 --> 07:47.509
Really?

07:48.010 --> 07:50.888
I heard the twins' dad got promoted.
Maybe that's why they moved.

07:50.971 --> 07:53.098
Well, he should've said goodbye.

07:54.141 --> 07:57.519
What about us? When can we move?

07:59.188 --> 08:00.564
Isn't it nice here?

08:01.148 --> 08:03.025
I turned down a promotion, huh?

08:03.108 --> 08:04.234
[chuckles]

08:07.779 --> 08:09.907
-That's right. Eat up.
-[Eui-ju chuckles]

08:15.746 --> 08:17.247
[whispers] Pervert!

08:21.251 --> 08:22.669
I think I'm done eating.

08:25.464 --> 08:26.715
Come on, eat some more.

08:26.798 --> 08:29.384
[Eui-ju] It's okay. I'll run late if I do.

08:31.011 --> 08:32.554
I'm off to school now.

08:33.972 --> 08:36.016
-[Ma] Bye! Be safe!
-[Shin] Careful on the road.

08:40.979 --> 08:42.564
I said I'd go by myself.

08:42.648 --> 08:45.025
Ah, come on, just listen to me.
Let's go together.

08:45.108 --> 08:47.736
That car air freshener smells awful.

08:48.487 --> 08:49.780
No, wait a second.

08:54.368 --> 08:55.953
I'm going with you.

08:56.036 --> 08:58.038
Forget it. Stay out of my business.

08:58.121 --> 08:59.414
What on earth?

08:59.498 --> 09:01.250
Aren't they the guys from yesterday?

09:01.333 --> 09:02.709
Hey, Woo-su!

09:06.338 --> 09:07.339
I can't do that.

09:09.633 --> 09:11.927
-You know I can't do that.
-That's enough!

09:12.010 --> 09:13.762
Oh, this is crazy.

09:14.388 --> 09:15.389
It's a hassle.

09:15.973 --> 09:16.974
[gasps] Couple fight?

09:17.557 --> 09:19.184
Please listen to me.

09:21.019 --> 09:23.230
How long do I have to listen to you for?

09:23.313 --> 09:25.565
Let's just take the car and make it easy.

09:25.649 --> 09:27.818
I don't wanna keep doing what you want.

09:27.901 --> 09:29.152
I'm saying I'll go alone.

09:29.236 --> 09:32.114
Ugh, that one's just a big jerk.
[clicks tongue]

09:32.197 --> 09:35.492
The others are almost ready.
Just give them a minute.

09:35.575 --> 09:37.911
Treating someone nice like that,

09:37.995 --> 09:39.538
he's just gonna regret it.

09:41.039 --> 09:42.916
-[chuckles]
-[mosquito buzzing]

09:43.500 --> 09:44.584
Ouch.

09:44.668 --> 09:45.961
Knock it off already.

09:46.044 --> 09:48.588
-Woo-su!
-Did it get on my face?

09:51.341 --> 09:52.467
[sighs]

09:56.430 --> 09:57.431
Hold on a second.

10:11.778 --> 10:14.031
[Eui-ju] Whoa. He's gorgeous!

10:15.282 --> 10:16.283
Were you filming?

10:18.618 --> 10:21.204
-What?
-I saw you filming us. Delete it.

10:21.288 --> 10:23.457
[stammers, sighs] No, I didn't.

10:23.540 --> 10:25.751
I was seeing if I got a bug on my face.

10:25.834 --> 10:26.918
[scoffs]

10:29.463 --> 10:32.924
Listen I'm not some kind of creep
who secretly films people on the street.

10:33.008 --> 10:35.719
I'll let it slide if you delete it,
all right? So choose carefully.

10:37.471 --> 10:38.805
I said that I didn't do it.

10:45.228 --> 10:47.230
-What's wrong?
-She was filming us.

10:47.898 --> 10:50.650
I bet she wants to post it
just to get comments.

10:53.612 --> 10:55.072
ZERO COMMENTS

10:58.784 --> 11:00.535
Just for comments?

11:02.120 --> 11:03.580
I do want comments!

11:03.663 --> 11:06.541
The more, the better.
I completely wrecked the ending.

11:06.625 --> 11:10.670
And I still… I still didn't even get
a single hate comment.

11:10.754 --> 11:12.881
Do you have any idea
how humiliating that is?

11:12.964 --> 11:14.424
A hundred episodes and nothing.

11:16.176 --> 11:17.844
-Oh, darn.
-Don't change the subject.

11:19.096 --> 11:20.555
That's enough.

11:20.639 --> 11:21.640
You really weren't filming?

11:22.224 --> 11:23.475
Mm-hmm.

11:23.558 --> 11:25.018
She said she wasn't.

11:25.102 --> 11:27.646
But I saw you, you were hiding
right there, filming us.

11:27.729 --> 11:28.772
[scoffs]

11:28.855 --> 11:30.899
-Give it to me, I'm checking.
-Oh, hey! What the heck?

11:30.982 --> 11:32.359
-What are you doing? Let go.
-Let go.

11:32.442 --> 11:33.777
-Come on, let go of it.
-Stop. Stop it.

11:33.860 --> 11:35.862
I didn't film anything. I didn't! [grunts]

11:36.696 --> 11:38.073
[exclaims]

11:40.450 --> 11:41.451
[gasps]

11:44.079 --> 11:46.206
[whimpering] No. No, no, no.

11:46.289 --> 11:49.084
No, please, no. Please, please.

11:49.709 --> 11:50.710
[gasps]

11:50.794 --> 11:52.379
Oh, no.

11:52.462 --> 11:54.423
[crying]

11:54.506 --> 11:56.967
You broke my phone! Are you serious?

11:57.050 --> 11:59.052
What are you gonna do about this?

11:59.136 --> 12:00.178
I can't believe this!

12:00.262 --> 12:02.347
You should've just let me
check your phone.

12:03.056 --> 12:04.850
[Dong-ju] Sorry about this, kid.

12:04.933 --> 12:06.893
He was overreacting
because he has past trauma

12:06.977 --> 12:08.728
from getting filmed
without his permission.

12:08.812 --> 12:10.605
We'll compensate you
for your broken phone.

12:10.689 --> 12:13.191
[breathing deeply]

12:13.275 --> 12:15.735
Forget it! Geez.

12:18.864 --> 12:20.907
You know why students wear uniforms?

12:25.162 --> 12:27.330
It's a way of identifying them.

12:27.414 --> 12:28.957
You better not spread
what you filmed today,

12:29.040 --> 12:31.835
or I'll teach you what it means
to regret doing something.

12:35.005 --> 12:36.089
Such an asshole!

12:38.008 --> 12:39.009
Hey!

12:39.509 --> 12:41.261
Why are you still here?

12:41.344 --> 12:43.221
We're running late. Come with us.

12:43.305 --> 12:44.514
Oh, wait. Wait a second.

12:47.100 --> 12:50.854
[K-pop music playing]

12:58.361 --> 12:59.696
Slow down.

13:24.804 --> 13:27.182
JEONJU MURIM GIRLS' HIGH

13:29.809 --> 13:33.188
CHAPTER 3:
SO, THAT ASSHOLE IS MY…

13:33.271 --> 13:35.232
[music continues]

13:37.901 --> 13:41.238
-Eui-ju! Yeo Eui-ju!
-Oh. [chuckles]

13:42.030 --> 13:43.865
[Eui-ju] This is my bestie, Choi Go-ya.

13:43.949 --> 13:45.075
She's an art talent,

13:45.158 --> 13:48.870
and she's always had a boyfriend,
ever since we were in sixth grade.

13:50.956 --> 13:54.292
I feel like I've gained at least 4 pounds
after all that sleeping and eating.

13:54.376 --> 13:55.585
[sighs]

13:56.836 --> 13:58.463
What the… What happened?

13:59.381 --> 14:01.383
This guy recently moved
into my neighborhood,

14:01.466 --> 14:03.843
and he thought I was filming him,
so he wanted to check my phone.

14:03.927 --> 14:05.679
I didn't let him take it
and this happened.

14:05.762 --> 14:06.763
Dang.

14:06.846 --> 14:08.265
And you let him get away with it?

14:08.348 --> 14:09.766
You should've demanded compensation

14:09.849 --> 14:12.060
or got his number
to make him pay the hard way!

14:12.143 --> 14:13.853
No. I didn't want to.

14:13.937 --> 14:16.398
-He looked like he had a nasty temper.
-[phone buzzing]

14:17.774 --> 14:18.942
[sighs]

14:19.776 --> 14:21.111
What? Who is that?

14:21.861 --> 14:22.862
My ex.

14:23.363 --> 14:24.906
You broke up again?

14:24.990 --> 14:27.867
Didn't you say he was the most
handsome guy at your academy?

14:30.620 --> 14:33.331
I wonder when I'll get to meet
my one true love.

14:34.207 --> 14:35.750
Lucky you.

14:35.834 --> 14:38.295
I haven't even had my first love yet.

14:38.378 --> 14:39.504
[sighs]

14:39.588 --> 14:43.758
Maybe my novels are boring
because I've never been in a relationship.

14:44.801 --> 14:45.802
Not true…

14:46.553 --> 14:48.471
Dating may help, but then…

14:49.306 --> 14:52.058
[groans] …it ruins your fantasies
the more you date.

14:53.059 --> 14:54.644
In your case you're better off writing,

14:54.728 --> 14:57.731
because you still fantasize
about dating and romance.

14:58.356 --> 14:59.608
You think?

14:59.691 --> 15:02.235
Hmm. What is it?
Do you have writer's block?

15:02.319 --> 15:03.945
You said you finished.

15:04.029 --> 15:06.072
I did. I finished it.

15:08.366 --> 15:10.535
When are you going to let me read them?

15:10.619 --> 15:12.704
You didn't tell me the titles
or your pen name.

15:13.371 --> 15:14.956
That's just too mean.

15:15.040 --> 15:17.667
I told you already.
I'm taking it to my grave.

15:18.251 --> 15:20.962
[chuckles] If it's a mega hit,

15:21.046 --> 15:22.922
are you going to keep it a secret then?

15:23.548 --> 15:24.549
Mega hit?

15:25.634 --> 15:28.261
Aw, you'll be the first
to hear the news, then.

15:28.345 --> 15:29.346
[both laughing]

15:29.429 --> 15:32.015
I really hope it comes true. A mega hit.

15:32.098 --> 15:33.892
[students chattering]

15:34.809 --> 15:36.394
[student 1] What are you guys looking at?

15:36.478 --> 15:37.812
[student 2] Go-ya! Eui-ju!

15:37.896 --> 15:39.856
-Hey, Eui-ju. Eui-ju, over here.
-Over here! Hurry!

15:39.939 --> 15:42.359
-Come on. Hurry!
-What's going on? I wanna know. Tell me.

15:42.442 --> 15:43.693
[clamoring]

15:44.653 --> 15:45.862
[student 3] Do you see them?

15:45.945 --> 15:48.406
Aw, they've finally come,
after all those rumors.

15:48.490 --> 15:50.659
-[student 2] Wow. [sighing]
-Dang, all the new teachers are men.

15:50.742 --> 15:52.952
But they're not just men.
They're drop-dead gorgeous men.

15:53.036 --> 15:55.038
Oh, this is seriously insane.

15:55.121 --> 15:57.832
Look, they're a solid ten,
a whole package. [sighs]

15:57.916 --> 16:02.212
I'm going crazy here. I'm going crazy.
I can't handle it.

16:02.295 --> 16:04.214
I've never wanted to enter
the teachers' office this much

16:04.297 --> 16:06.633
in my whole life. [moans]

16:08.009 --> 16:10.845
[student 2] Young-hee said we were
not allowed in and locked the doors.

16:11.721 --> 16:13.973
Why wouldn't she let the students watch
the new teachers

16:14.057 --> 16:16.017
-introduce themselves?
-[student 3] I know.

16:16.101 --> 16:17.852
That's Jung Gi-jeon.

16:17.936 --> 16:18.978
JUNG GI-JEON

16:19.062 --> 16:21.231
He's a PE teacher.
He used to be a national athlete.

16:21.314 --> 16:24.484
He was the first Korean to place fourth
in the luge at the Winter Games.

16:24.567 --> 16:28.029
Oh, dang. Look at him. [gasps] Wow.

16:28.113 --> 16:30.907
That's Noh Da-ju. He's multilingual.

16:30.990 --> 16:33.076
He's gonna teach Japanese
and first-grade Spanish.

16:33.159 --> 16:34.536
[in Spanish] When I was six…

16:35.453 --> 16:37.455
[student 3, in English]
He made a speech at the TUD Talk

16:37.539 --> 16:39.457
titled Secret to Conquering
Foreign Languages.

16:39.541 --> 16:42.585
And rumor says he's the youngest son
of a filthy-rich family.

16:43.712 --> 16:45.714
I'm so glad I'm here today.

16:50.093 --> 16:54.305
[student 3] Oh. That's Yoon Dong-ju,
a Korean literature teacher.

16:54.389 --> 16:57.976
What's that poem he published through
Literary Youth in 2020? "My Mother"?

17:00.019 --> 17:01.020
I found him.

17:02.897 --> 17:04.357
My true love.

17:06.651 --> 17:08.653
Hold on a second.

17:09.571 --> 17:11.531
He's a Korean literature teacher?

17:11.614 --> 17:13.616
[gasps] There's no way.

17:14.409 --> 17:15.952
It can't be.

17:16.035 --> 17:18.997
This is Ga Woo-su. Our new math teacher.

17:21.666 --> 17:25.754
So. Thanks to his outstanding
research accomplishments in college,

17:25.837 --> 17:29.716
he was offered positions
by several Ivy League universities

17:29.799 --> 17:33.011
but he decided to join us here.

17:33.928 --> 17:36.389
-[stammers]
-["Symphony No. 5 in C Minor" playing]

17:36.473 --> 17:38.099
[Eui-ju] Isn't he that jerk?

17:39.350 --> 17:41.060
He's a Mensa member.

17:41.144 --> 17:43.146
-You heard her, right?
-[staff applauding]

17:43.229 --> 17:44.898
He's a Mensa member.

17:44.981 --> 17:48.902
So in a few words, he's a math genius.

17:48.985 --> 17:51.112
[staff cheering, applauding]

17:51.196 --> 17:53.114
[students clamoring]

17:53.740 --> 17:55.700
[screaming]

17:55.784 --> 17:57.744
[music continues]

18:06.711 --> 18:08.671
[all exclaim]

18:12.425 --> 18:14.511
[no audible dialogue]

18:40.119 --> 18:41.746
Sorry, I dropped my phone.

18:41.830 --> 18:42.956
[chuckles] Sorry.

18:45.750 --> 18:46.751
[music ends]

18:46.835 --> 18:48.878
Oh, my goodness. Did you guys see them?

18:48.962 --> 18:51.214
I'm going for Da-ju.
He's my one and only pick.

18:51.297 --> 18:53.007
The era of Ha E-den is long gone now.

18:53.091 --> 18:55.218
Hey, don't you compare him to them, girl.

18:55.301 --> 18:57.262
We've adored him only because he's cute.

18:57.345 --> 18:58.596
[laughs]

18:58.680 --> 19:01.599
Were you talking about me?
This early in the day?

19:02.892 --> 19:04.519
HA E-DEN
MUSIC TEACHER

19:04.602 --> 19:07.689
-[chuckles]
-[chuckles] No, we weren't.

19:07.772 --> 19:11.651
[scoffs] Go-ya. How cold.
You hurt my feelings.

19:11.734 --> 19:14.362
Thank you for filling in for
our homeroom teacher.

19:14.946 --> 19:16.698
[all] Thank you very much.

19:18.575 --> 19:20.243
-What the--
-[student 3 chuckles]

19:23.204 --> 19:24.330
-Good morning.
-What on earth…

19:24.414 --> 19:26.207
-Good morning.
-No, it's not good.

19:26.291 --> 19:28.543
-Good morning.
-Have they lost their minds altogether?

19:30.336 --> 19:31.796
[students chattering]

19:33.840 --> 19:37.927
MURIM GIRL'S HIGH
11TH GRADE CLASS 2

19:39.679 --> 19:42.515
I'm going to wear full makeup
every day from now on.

19:42.599 --> 19:44.309
Who's your favorite one?

19:45.059 --> 19:46.936
Mr. Dong-ju. [laughs]

19:47.020 --> 19:49.230
-He's my husband.
-[both laughing]

19:49.314 --> 19:51.649
What should I major in
to become a devoted wife?

19:51.733 --> 19:54.694
Mr. Yoon seems to prefer
a docile type, though.

19:56.696 --> 19:58.948
My-My pick is the Japanese teacher, okay?

19:59.032 --> 20:01.284
Go back to what you were doing.
There, there.

20:03.453 --> 20:04.996
-Who did you pick?
-For what?

20:05.079 --> 20:06.873
Your crush? That's what I meant.

20:06.956 --> 20:07.957
We shouldn't overlap.

20:08.041 --> 20:10.460
Whatever, I don't care
about choosing a crush.

20:11.044 --> 20:13.379
But Mr. Yoon isn't your type, though.

20:13.463 --> 20:14.672
-I changed.
-Mmm.

20:15.715 --> 20:17.675
-[both chuckle]
-Wait. Uh, uh. Hold on.

20:18.426 --> 20:20.845
-I just got goose bumps.
-Why? What is it?

20:20.929 --> 20:23.514
Wait, listen,
this means one of them… [gasps]

20:23.598 --> 20:26.768
…is going to be our homeroom teacher.

20:26.851 --> 20:29.896
-[squealing] Sweet!
-[squealing] This is insane!

20:29.979 --> 20:31.230
[student 4] Shut up!

20:35.068 --> 20:38.029
EUN HA-SU
TOP OF THE SCHOOL, PRESENCE

20:38.112 --> 20:39.489
Keep it down, will you?

20:40.615 --> 20:42.033
[clears throat]

20:42.116 --> 20:43.743
Class hasn't started yet.

20:43.826 --> 20:46.371
Yes, but at least don't disturb others.

20:49.916 --> 20:51.292
[softly] As if she owns this class.

20:52.669 --> 20:54.671
You're low on sugar, aren't you?

20:54.754 --> 20:56.464
How about a cafeteria run?

20:59.592 --> 21:00.593
Where are you going?

21:00.677 --> 21:02.720
[K-pop music playing]

21:06.724 --> 21:08.643
BRACKET BY SPORT

21:08.726 --> 21:10.853
KOREAN LITERATURE TIMETABLE

21:10.937 --> 21:12.105
MR. GA WOO-SU

21:12.188 --> 21:15.441
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH
11TH GRADE TEACHERS' OFFICE

21:15.525 --> 21:17.610
[music continues]

21:22.156 --> 21:24.909
[camera shutter clicking]

21:36.963 --> 21:39.298
KOREAN LITERATURE TIMETABLE

21:41.926 --> 21:44.012
Dong-ju, are you coloring right now?

21:45.054 --> 21:47.390
Oh. [chuckles]
I won't get confused this way.

21:48.099 --> 21:49.100
[chuckles]

21:51.394 --> 21:52.395
[sighs]

21:52.478 --> 21:53.896
Feeling okay?

21:53.980 --> 21:55.523
Do you need anything?

21:55.606 --> 21:58.026
No, thanks.
I should be getting better soon.

22:02.697 --> 22:03.698
Darn it.

22:15.585 --> 22:16.586
[sighs]

22:17.211 --> 22:19.005
Did you come here to clean?

22:19.088 --> 22:20.298
Knock it off.

22:20.381 --> 22:21.466
Leave me alone.

22:22.800 --> 22:26.512
[sighs] In this jungle-like society,
standing out means death.

22:26.596 --> 22:30.183
You're just a clueless kid who
doesn't understand how the world works.

22:30.808 --> 22:33.728
-Let's change desks. I can't stand him.
-Oh, please.

22:34.479 --> 22:36.856
I'd love to stay here in front of you.

22:36.939 --> 22:39.442
I miss you even when I'm seeing you.

22:39.525 --> 22:41.819
Just settle for it. It's been decided.

22:41.903 --> 22:44.739
-I don't want to face this bat every day.
-What?

22:51.788 --> 22:53.414
I told you not to call me that.

22:54.540 --> 22:56.250
I hate hearing that word.

22:56.334 --> 22:58.920
It's like "Voldemort" to me,
you understand?

22:59.003 --> 23:00.880
Don't you know it disgusts me? Mm-mm-mmm.

23:00.963 --> 23:03.257
Oh, yes, you do. There's no freaking way

23:03.341 --> 23:06.344
that the genius Ga Woo-su
wouldn't remember it.

23:09.639 --> 23:11.516
My hippocampus is not like yours.

23:11.599 --> 23:13.684
It not only takes part
in learning and memory,

23:13.768 --> 23:15.144
but also in emotional control,

23:15.686 --> 23:18.022
which is why I can't stand facing you.

23:20.066 --> 23:21.651
No. No, no, no.

23:22.276 --> 23:24.112
Don't humiliate me.

23:24.195 --> 23:25.613
You memory freak!

23:25.696 --> 23:26.864
Hey, fruit bat!

23:26.948 --> 23:28.074
What? You four-eyed nerd?

23:28.157 --> 23:30.076
-Four-eyed nerd?
-Darn you…

23:30.159 --> 23:31.494
[Dong-ju] That's enough already.

23:32.453 --> 23:35.039
[intercom beeping]

23:38.209 --> 23:39.293
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

23:39.377 --> 23:42.213
Hmm. [sighs] How can you be sure
that Mr. Yoon is your true love?

23:42.296 --> 23:44.549
You've only just met him.

23:44.632 --> 23:45.800
Hmm.

23:45.883 --> 23:46.884
Love is like…

23:47.969 --> 23:50.388
first snow. Right in that moment,

23:50.471 --> 23:54.851
when you see them,
oh, you just have this feeling.

23:55.601 --> 23:57.145
And you know they're the one.

23:57.937 --> 24:00.731
And it always comes
when you least expect it.

24:02.817 --> 24:06.404
So then, does that mean
that all your countless ex-boyfriends

24:06.487 --> 24:08.573
weren't your first snow, Choi Go-ya?

24:09.323 --> 24:11.993
I thought they were,
but they turned out to be frost.

24:12.785 --> 24:13.828
[chuckles]

24:13.911 --> 24:16.664
My first snow actually came today.

24:17.748 --> 24:18.749
[chuckles]

24:18.833 --> 24:21.586
And when will I get my first snow, then?

24:22.587 --> 24:23.588
I told you.

24:24.213 --> 24:26.716
It comes when you least expect it to.

24:27.758 --> 24:28.759
It hits you

24:29.677 --> 24:31.095
out of nowhere

24:31.846 --> 24:33.890
-before you can react. Bam!
-[student] Thank you.

24:33.973 --> 24:35.600
-Ouch!
-[cashier] No problem. See you.

24:35.683 --> 24:37.476
[laughs]

24:37.560 --> 24:39.437
-How much is it?
-One thirty-three.

24:40.313 --> 24:41.981
-[both] Thank you.
-No problem.

24:42.773 --> 24:43.941
Lucky you.

24:44.025 --> 24:46.402
While one new teacher
has become your first snow,

24:46.485 --> 24:48.404
I got involved with another
in a messed-up way.

24:48.487 --> 24:50.698
-[Go-ya laughs]
-Ugh, whatever.

24:51.324 --> 24:52.742
[sighs] Well.

24:53.910 --> 24:57.914
Come to think of it, this must be why
he mentioned school uniforms and stuff.

24:57.997 --> 24:59.165
[scoffs]

24:59.248 --> 25:03.753
So what if he's a genius?
He has a shitty personality. Ugh.

25:05.546 --> 25:08.049
[romantic music playing]

25:12.553 --> 25:13.930
-[Go-ya] What is it?
-[music stops]

25:16.015 --> 25:17.475
[whimpering]

25:18.726 --> 25:22.396
[door creaking]

25:22.480 --> 25:24.482
[romantic music resumes]

25:42.208 --> 25:43.834
[music stops]

25:45.795 --> 25:47.588
[rock music playing]

25:47.672 --> 25:49.215
NO WAY

25:49.298 --> 25:51.801
I'M YOUR HOMEROOM TEACHER

25:59.183 --> 26:00.393
[exhales sharply]
